I haven't made any edits, because I can't see `app/src/invoices.ts` and any edit would be a guess. A SEARCH block has to match the file exactly once, and I don't know how `Invoice.pay` is written. I also don't know how payments are stored (the field name), what shape a payment has (whether the reference is `reference`, `ref` or something else), or what `pay` returns. Rewriting the whole file would risk destroying code I can't see, and appending a wrapper at the end would rest on the same unknowns.

Please paste the `Invoice` class, or at least `pay` along with the payment type and the field that holds recorded payments. I'll then return an exact edit.

The change I plan is a check at the top of `pay`, before anything is recorded or taken, and after any existing validation so that calls that throw today still throw:

```ts
if (payment.reference !== "") {
  const key = payment.reference.toLowerCase();
  if (this.payments.some(p => p.reference.toLowerCase() === key)) {
    return /* whatever "nothing taken" looks like in this method */;
  }
}
```

- **Case only:** it uses plain `toLowerCase()` with no trimming or accent folding, so `" bacs-17"` and `"bacs-é17"` stay distinct references.
- **Empty references:** they are never refused.
- **Recorded payments:** they keep the reference exactly as given.

What the refused branch should return depends on the current return type, which is why I need the code.
